{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Gerry the Squirrel is at a corner of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8e44ac5dbe890daf86ba3414fbfb7ccd80dfa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\times9$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> grid. An acorn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is placed. There are four coins placed randomly on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c761a8cba76f97f996ae3431b5d1de50c32e00d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\times 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid. Gerry will go the shortest path to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, and if there are multiple shortest paths, Gerry will pick one randomly. Given that Gerry does not start on top of a coin, the acorn is not on a coin, find the expected value of coins Gerry passes during his trip to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Place Gerry at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose the acorn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is located at  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6259a7672e8dd28156c69835ec7c51c094e927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le x,y\\le 8,(x,y)\\neq(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" /> (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible positions). Any shortest path from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946c2538d06e0fa0de538b309c43ed932897f619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> lattice points. So, the expected number of points Gerry passes through is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db847a47b84b85a85fab1d039a1351579dad623e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sum_{x=0}^8\\sum_{y=0}^8(x+y-1)-(0+0-1)}{80}=\\frac{81\\cdot(4+4-1)+1}{80}=\\frac{568}{80}.\\]\" width=\"524\" height=\"44\" /> The four coins are placed randomly among the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8b908d15627ea3a118bb38668d865edf722170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> remaining lattice points. Hence, each point Gerry passes has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c71717091b4b0d4504af61efa3fbdb35326893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{79}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> probability of containing a coin. So, the expected number of coins Gerry passes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5b37f7d534e59126fa8776e142896948b1c13b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{568}{80}\\cdot\\frac{4}{79}=\\frac{142}{395}\\implies 142+395=\\boxed{537}.\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017160517\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 86/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3791/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31925:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017160517 and revision id 274654. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}